WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.850
This is VisionRedact Studio, blurring
faces in 4K video, live.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:07.860
Courts, police, CCTV, schools and
newsrooms

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.167
often hide faces before sharing video,

4
00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.959
and by hand, that's every face in every
frame.

5
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.397
I built it in C# and WPF, and when you
hover over the timeline,

6
00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:19.499
a preview appears straight away.

7
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.883
A YOLO model finds the faces on my
laptop's GPU, nothing goes to the cloud,

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.470
and the boxes follow people as they move.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.810
Every face it finds starts out blurred,
and it is only shown if I reject it.

10
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:46.630
It can also group faces into people, right
on the device.

11
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.290
And if it misses someone, I can draw a
box, and the box follows them.

12
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.941
It plays 4K at sixty frames a second with
the blur on,

13
00:00:59.941 --> 00:01:02.390
and the app measures itself as it runs.

14
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.746
Export writes every frame, leaves the
original untouched,

15
00:01:08.746 --> 00:01:11.210
and tells you exactly what it checked.

16
00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:17.330
I'll show how I built it, starting with
smooth 4K60 video in WPF.

